fect is oracle-side and was\\nalready fixed for `493390fc03979205` (grow `ENDOR_RESULT_MAX` to 16 KiB + skip\\nhonestly when a result still overflows the buffer); at the standing branch the\\noracle now captures the full 1128-byte result (`result_truncated=false`, under\\nthe 16 KiB buffer) and both engines agree. Confirmed: the input crashes on the\\n`llm` base (old 1024-byte buffer) and checks clean on the standing branch.\\n\\nNo engine/port/oracle code changed — the fix already covers this input. This\\ncommit adds a load-bearing regression lock so the exact input stays covered:\\n\\n- ironhorse-fuzz: replay the exact 4 bytes through the real\\n  `differential_check_with_symbols` and assert no divergence (fails if the\\n  oracle buffer fix is reverted).\\n- ironhorse-vm: replay the finding's program as frozen bytecode+symbols (no XS\\n  oracle / no c/moddable submodule) and assert the port renders the whole\\n  1128-byte result without panicking or truncating.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock regexp .toString() truncation (…\",\"oid\":\"e29083075d477a185b0a001a492f9251f04d1076\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:21:11Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:21:18Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…15d6d93)\\n\\nThe continuous-Ironhorse-fuzz `differential_source` arm flagged a \\\"result\\\"\\ndivergence on the 5-byte input `e1 1b dc dc dc` (sha256 203db557…449e2),\\nwhich the structure-aware generator folds into the arithmetic program\\n\\n    ((-(-(-226492416))) * (-(-(-226492416))))\\n\\nThe literal `226492416` is the generator's \\\"larger integer\\\" atom `27 << 23`;\\nthe triple unary minus collapses to a single negate, so the program is\\n`(-226492416) * (-226492416) = 226492416^2 = (27*2^23)^2 = 729 * 2^46`, the\\nexactly-representable double whose real value is `51298814505517056`.\\n\\nReproduced against the pinned XS oracle (moddable 23b4d6b): XS's `fx_dtoa`\\nrenders the exact integer `51298814505517056` (17 digits) while ironhorse —\\nlike V8/SpiderMonkey and ECMA-262 §6.1.6.1.20's \\\"let k be as small as\\npossible\\\" — renders the shortest round-tripping decimal `51298814505517060`\\n(verified byte-identical to Node/V8). Both spellings parse back to the same\\ndouble, so the port was never wrong; ironhorse is the spec-conformant one.\\n\\nSame class as finding `d99d263fcf6ca7a7`: the differential harness already\\ncompares numeric completions by their IEEE-754 double rather than their\\ndecimal spelling (`results_agree`), so this input is already suppressed on the\\nstanding branch — no port or harness change is required. This change is\\nregression-only:\\n\\n  - `ironhorse-vm/tests/finding_5c29667cc15d6d93_large_integer_dtoa.rs`: the\\n    CI-visible, submodule-free regression — pins the port's own\\n    `number_to_ecma_string(729*2^46) == \\\"51298814505517060\\\"` so the port can\\n    never be \\\"corrected\\\" to XS's non-conformant exact-integer spelling. (The\\n    engine's CI runs only `cargo test -p ironhorse-vm -p ironhorse-snapshot`;\\n    the oracle-linked crates need the c/moddable submodule and are excluded.)\\n  - `ironhorse-fuzz` test `finding_5c29667cc15d6d93_large_integer_dtoa_agrees`:\\n    replays the exact bytes through `gen_program` + `differential_check` and\\n    asserts no divergence (oracle-verified; needs the submodule).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): pin large-integer dtoa spelling (fuzz 5c29667cc…\",\"oid\":\"a2733761a57ab603cf9a6869aff2f7116a8ec596\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:23:47Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:24:37Z\",\"messageBody\":\"… a136f9038a1001fb)\\n\\nThe continuous Ironhorse fuzz target `differential_regexp_surface` reproduced a\\ncrash on the 5-byte input `2c 2c 2c d4 88` (sha256\\nd3bc62680a221ff9518c4aad6b03787bded65b75091e3b1dd34b1451e7a5835c), which the\\nstructure-aware generator folds into a deeply nested\\n`new RegExp(<pattern>, \\\"m\\\").source`. The completion value is a 1955-byte string.\\n\\nThis is a distinct minimized input of the SAME class as findings\\n`493390fc03979205` and `3ea435c58b4c588e`: the pre-fix XS differential oracle\\ncaptured the completion value into a fixed 1024-byte buffer and truncated it to\\n1023 bytes, so the harness read the port's *correct* full 1955-byte result as a\\ndivergence and panicked. The port was never wrong. The two prior inputs reached\\nthe long result via `.toString()`; this one reaches it via the `.source`\\naccessor (generator selector 4), a distinct fold. The causal defect is\\noracle-side and was already fixed for `493390fc03979205` (grow `ENDOR_RESULT_MAX`\\nto 16 KiB + skip honestly when a result still overflows the buffer); at the\\nstanding branch the oracle now captures the full 1955-byte result\\n(`result_truncated=false`, well under the 16 KiB buffer) and both engines agree.\\nConfirmed: the input crashes on the `llm` base (38ca1d189, old 1024-byte buffer)\\nwith a truncated oracle result vs the port's full 1955 bytes, and checks clean on\\nthe standing branch.\\n\\nNo engine/port/oracle code changed — the fix already covers this input. This\\ncommit adds a load-bearing regression lock so the exact input stays covered\\n(`fuzz/corpus` and `fuzz/artifacts` are gitignored, so a corpus seed is not a\\npermanent regression):\\n\\n- ironhorse-fuzz: replay the exact 5 bytes through the real\\n  `differential_check_with_symbols` and assert no divergence (fails if the\\n  oracle buffer fix is reverted).\\n- ironhorse-vm: replay the finding's program as frozen bytecode+symbols (no XS\\n  oracle / no c/moddable submodule) and assert the port renders the whole\\n  1955-byte result without panicking or truncating.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock regexp .source truncation (fuzz…\",\"oid\":\"cd9c3251a93960f4a5514763a8e9964c4a1daa20\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:35:59Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:35:59Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…3d074ec)\\n\\nThe continuous-Ironhorse-fuzz `differential_source` arm flagged a \\\"result\\\"\\ndivergence on the 4-byte input `d8 7f 33 ba`\\n(sha256 6abb2fe734124222bc19e12518fa968a59f254edea3c9ed262414cb4637c736f),\\nwhich the structure-aware generator folds into the arithmetic program\\n\\n    ((~(~(1560281088 * true))) * ((~(1560281088 * true)) << ((~true) << (true << true))))\\n\\nThe literal `1560281088` is the generator's \\\"larger integer\\\" atom `186 << 23`.\\nIn ToInt32 arithmetic the left factor is `1560281088`, the outer shift count is\\n`(~true) << (true << true) = -8` (taken mod 32 → 24), the right factor is\\n`(~1560281088) << 24 = -16777216`, and the product is\\n`1560281088 * -16777216 = -(186 * 2^47) = -(93 * 2^48)`, the exactly-representable\\ndouble whose real value is `-26177172834091008` (magnitude overflows 2^53).\\n\\nReproduced against the pinned XS oracle (moddable 23b4d6b): XS's `fx_dtoa`\\nrenders the exact integer `-26177172834091008` (17 digits) while ironhorse —\\nlike V8/SpiderMonkey and ECMA-262 §6.1.6.1.20's \\\"let k be as small as\\npossible\\\" — renders the shortest round-tripping decimal `-26177172834091010`\\n(verified byte-identical to Node/V8). Both spellings parse back to the same\\ndouble, so the port was never wrong; ironhorse is the spec-conformant one.\\n\\nSame class as findings `d99d263fcf6ca7a7` and `5c29667cc15d6d93`: the\\ndifferential harness already compares numeric completions by their IEEE-754\\ndouble rather than their decimal spelling (`results_agree`), so this input is\\nalready suppressed on the standing branch — no port or harness change is\\nrequired. This change is regression-only:\\n\\n  - `ironhorse-vm/tests/finding_7289e31013d074ec_large_integer_dtoa.rs`: the\\n    CI-visible, submodule-free regression — pins the port's own\\n    `number_to_ecma_string(-(93*2^48)) == \\\"-26177172834091010\\\"` so the port can\\n    never be \\\"corrected\\\" to XS's non-conformant exact-integer spelling. (The\\n    engine's CI runs only `cargo test -p ironhorse-vm -p ironhorse-snapshot`;\\n    the oracle-linked crates need the c/moddable submodule and are excluded.)\\n  - `ironhorse-fuzz` test `finding_7289e31013d074ec_large_integer_dtoa_agrees`:\\n    replays the exact bytes through `gen_program` + `differential_check` and\\n    asserts no divergence (oracle-verified; needs the submodule).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): pin large-integer dtoa spelling (fuzz 7289e3101…\",\"oid\":\"098f7ab017aee42f3b6ca35207200e5a71ce7746\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:41:02Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:41:07Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…flow (fuzz 407764ab1120ed1a)\\n\\nThe continuous-Ironhorse-fuzz `differential_regexp` arm re-surfaced a \\\"match\\nmeter\\\" divergence on a 3-byte input (sha256 233ee70c…e42c131, bytes `14 7f 5c`)\\nthat folds into a deeply nested, backreference-heavy pattern (capturing groups\\nplus `\\\\2`, `\\\\4`, `\\\\8`, `\\\\11`, … references to optional/unset groups) with the\\n`s` flag over \\\"abbab\\\"@1. Matching it dispatches 330041 metered steps, so the raw\\n16.16 match meter is 330041*65536 = 21_629_566_976 — past 2^32.\\n\\nThis is the same harness-side class as finding 5d122a6fc10babd9: the port meters\\ninto a `u64` and holds the full value; the XS oracle originally copied the pin's\\n64-bit `meterIndex` into a 32-bit `txU4` field and wrapped it to\\n21_629_566_976 mod 2^32 = 154_730_496, a phantom divergence against the port's\\ncorrect figure. That oracle-side truncation was already fixed (c8497fd8, widening\\nthe regexp meter fields to 64 bit end to end); the fuzzer re-found the class only\\nbecause it fuzzes the `llm` base branch, which predates the fix, so no new engine\\nor oracle change is warranted here.\\n\\nThe case is nonetheless distinct in shape from 5d122a6fc10babd9 — that one used\\nonly non-capturing groups; this one is dominated by quantified backreferences to\\nunset captures — so it independently guards the backreference dispatch path\\nagainst a silently narrowed meter.\\n\\nRegression (ironhorse-vm, builds without the oracle or the c/moddable submodule):\\n`finding_407764ab1120ed1a_regexp_meter_overflow` replays the exact generated\\npattern through the port's `compile`+`match_regexp`, asserting no panic and the\\nfull-width meter (330041*65536 > u32::MAX), pinned bit-exact so a 32-bit wrap\\nwould fail it.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock backref-heavy regexp meter over…\",\"oid\":\"410f3cb215e818c063145964389a18627fd7b2be\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:44:03Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T06:45:08Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…zz 783be6e6106bad98)\\n\\nThe continuous-Ironhorse-fuzz `differential_source` arm flagged a \\\"result\\\"\\ndivergence on the 6-byte input `00 00 66 69 27 44` (sha256\\n95c5064e49e6c191f7f9b8be24270555d12b04c226cbc72c01406e024ff39008), which the\\nstructure-aware generator folds into\\n\\n    ((((true + 327155712) && (!true)) || ((~570425344) * (true + 327155712)))\\n     + (!((570425344 || true) + (327155712 * -128))))\\n\\nThe `&&` is `false`, so the `||` takes its right operand; the outer `!(...)` is\\n`false` and coerces to `0` under `+`. The whole program collapses to the single\\nproduct `(~570425344) * (327155712 + 1) = -570425345 * 327155713`. Its exact\\nvalue `-186617910456745985` overflows 2^53 and rounds to the double\\n`-186617910456745984`.\\n\\nReproduced against the pinned XS oracle (moddable 23b4d6b) at the fuzz project\\nSHA 38ca1d189: XS's `fx_dtoa` renders a non-shortest 17-digit form\\n`-186617910456745980` while ironhorse — like V8/SpiderMonkey and ECMA-262\\n§6.1.6.1.20's \\\"let k be as small as possible\\\" — renders the shortest\\nround-tripping decimal `-186617910456746000` (verified byte-identical to\\nNode/V8). Both spellings parse back to the same double, so the port was never\\nwrong; ironhorse is the spec-conformant one.\\n\\nSame class as findings `d99d263fcf6ca7a7` and `5c29667cc15d6d93`: the\\ndifferential harness already compares numeric completions by their IEEE-754\\ndouble rather than their decimal spelling (`results_agree`), so this input is\\nalready suppressed on the standing branch — no port or harness change is\\nrequired. This change is regression-only:\\n\\n  - `ironhorse-vm/tests/finding_783be6e6106bad98_large_integer_dtoa.rs`: the\\n    CI-visible, submodule-free regression — pins the port's own\\n    `number_to_ecma_string(-570425345 * 327155713) == \\\"-186617910456746000\\\"`\\n    so the port can never be \\\"corrected\\\" to XS's non-shortest spelling. (The\\n    engine's CI runs only `cargo test -p ironhorse-vm -p ironhorse-snapshot`;\\n    the oracle-linked crates need the c/moddable submodule and are excluded.)\\n  - `ironhorse-fuzz` test `finding_783be6e6106bad98_large_integer_dtoa_agrees`:\\n    replays the exact 6 bytes through `gen_program` + `differential_check` and\\n    asserts no divergence (oracle-verified; needs the submodule).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock large-integer dtoa spelling (fu…\",\"oid\":\"d53328f8886b914b1130f7f1a958ab48ea912cd6\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T07:01:59Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T07:02:08Z\",\"messageBody\":\"… ab889c8f6184c60d)\\n\\nThe continuous Ironhorse fuzz target differential_regexp_surface reproduced a result divergence at the pinned llm SHA on a 4-byte minimized input (sha256 e31b5a31b...0412e07). The structure-aware generator produces a deeply nested RegExp source-accessor program whose completion value is 1216 bytes.\\n\\nThis is a distinct input of the same oracle-side class fixed by 7fae4aea2f: the old 1024-byte result buffer truncated XS output to 1023 bytes while ironhorse correctly returned the full value. The standing fix grows the buffer and skips honestly if a result still exceeds it, so no further production change is needed.\\n\\nAdd an exact-input differential regression and a submodule-free ironhorse-vm replay using frozen bytecode and symbols. Restoring the old buffer and disabling overflow detection makes the differential test fail with the original divergence; restoring the fix makes both regressions pass.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock regexp .source truncation (fuzz…\",\"oid\":\"3ef146edee61af42de2f1a7d7a68beafe57cf353\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T07:11:56Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T07:12:03Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…275793bca439f6e)\\n\\nThe continuous-Ironhorse-fuzz `differential_regexp` arm reported a \\\"match\\nmeter\\\" divergence on a 20-byte input (sha256 15296cb0…3e7a1e) that folds,\\nthrough `ironhorse_fuzz::gen_regexp`, into a backreference-heavy pathological\\npattern (nested empty-matchable `\\\\1*`/`\\\\3*` backrefs, lazy `\\\\1+?` /\\n`\\\\3*\\\\3*\\\\1+?` quantifiers, `{2}` repeats) over the subject \\\"0\\\"@0. The whole\\nmatch is just the leading `.` ((0,1)), but reaching it dispatches 1_120_070\\nmetered steps, so the raw 16.16 match meter is 1_120_070*65536 =\\n73_404_907_520 — 17x past 2^32.\\n\\nRoot cause: this is the SAME 32-bit-meter-truncation class as findings\\n493390fc03979205 and 5d122a6fc10babd9, already resolved on this branch by\\nwidening the XS oracle's meter fields to txU8 (commit c8497fd88). The port's\\nmatcher always metered into a u64 and held the full value; op-for-op the port\\nand the XS pin dispatch the identical 1_120_070-step histogram. Confirmed by\\nrebuilding the widened oracle and re-running the exact case: port and pin\\nagree bit-exact (matched, captures, and the full-width meter). The finding\\nonly \\\"reproduces\\\" against the base SHA 38ca1d189384245dd9accfcc2f79763a3b8ec5cb\\n(base `llm`) whose oracle predates c8497fd88 and wraps the meter to\\n73_404_907_520 mod 2^32 = 390_463_488 (5958 computrons), the phantom \\\"pin\\\"\\nvalue. No new port or oracle change is needed.\\n\\nRegression: ironhorse-vm `finding_8275793bca439f6e_regexp_meter_overflow`\\nreplays the exact generated pattern through the port's compile+match_regexp,\\nasserting no panic, the whole-match (0,1), and the full-width meter\\n(73_404_907_520 > u32::MAX, and not the 390_463_488 wrap). It is a DISTINCT,\\nbackreference-driven witness of the class (the sibling 5d122a6fc10babd9 case\\nuses only empty-star alternation, no backreferences), so it independently\\nguards the matcher against ever silently narrowing the meter. Builds without\\nthe oracle or the c/moddable submodule, per the standing-branch convention.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock regexp meter full-width (fuzz 8…\",\"oid\":\"bb42765fc1e1b6c67963f2bef5aae54de4ee84ee\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T09:34:55Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T09:34:55Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…8c673)\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock dtoa spelling (fuzz 66facfd52ae…\",\"oid\":\"13ae6c6f7b18cc405260eeb5e53a163988a4f3f4\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T09:44:03Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T09:44:35Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…03a7b)\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock dtoa spelling (fuzz 67a52af412f…\",\"oid\":\"54089e53f394e6659cd00da8b7e0df7869dcf6bd\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-30T10:58:08Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-30T10:58:08Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…2276f4edebdcb3bb)\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock regexp source truncation (fuzz …\",\"oid\":\"c2466f49c28fed0a0d210606f0319fa675080c2e\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T02:42:25Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T02:42:25Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The RegExp source getter must reuse the constructor source key when no escaping is required. Charging a fresh string chunk pushed this exact finding from 36 oracle computrons to 37 port computrons even though the result agreed.\\n\\nAdd the exact 6-byte minimized input plus frozen bytecode, symbols, and result as a submodule-free ironhorse-vm regression.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(ironhorse-vm): reuse unescaped regexp source (fuzz 1898f584e9bf841a)\",\"oid\":\"dbdddec7665803c54ebee6d3dd98745c0b0c10e9\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:05:53Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:05:53Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…n (fuzz 314f811064b8febb)\\n\\nThe 5-byte differential_source input \\\"ult{-\\\" folds into\\n(377487360 / (377487360 / (377487360 / (-5 / 981467136)))), whose value is\\nthe exactly-representable double 0xc370740000000000. XS's fx_dtoa renders it\\n-74098287619080190; ironhorse renders the ECMA-262 shortest round-tripping\\n-74098287619080200. Both parse to the same double, so the harness must agree\\n(the results_agree value comparison from finding d99d263fcf6ca7a7 already\\nsuppresses it). Same dtoa class, reached through division rather than a product.\\n\\n- ironhorse-fuzz: replays the exact bytes through differential_check and asserts\\n  no divergence (load-bearing: verified to FAIL if results_agree is reverted).\\n- ironhorse-vm: pins number_to_ecma_string for the finding value to the shortest\\n  decimal (no XS oracle / no c/moddable submodule; the regression CI runs).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock dtoa spelling via division chai…\",\"oid\":\"554bd7556ab1c790bcb3d22981bb909b65276dbb\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:08:44Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:08:50Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…z 5565a021a8cc30bc)\\n\\nThe continuous-Ironhorse-fuzz `differential_regexp` arm reported a \\\"match\\nmeter\\\" divergence on a 4-byte input (sha256 473e9934…88bc93) that folds,\\nthrough `ironhorse_fuzz::gen_regexp`, into a deeply nested, 44-group\\nbackreference-heavy alternation (forward backrefs like `\\\\12`/`\\\\39`, lazy\\n`\\\\w*?` runs, `{1,2}`/`{2}` repeats) over the subject \\\"b 0bb\\\"@0 with the `s`\\nflag. The pattern does NOT match, but the exhaustive backtrack to prove the\\nnon-match dispatches 128_348 metered steps, so the raw 16.16 match meter is\\n128_348*65536 = 8_411_414_528 — nearly 2x past 2^32.\\n\\nRoot cause: this is the SAME 32-bit-meter-truncation class as findings\\n493390fc03979205, 5d122a6fc10babd9, and 8275793bca439f6e, already resolved\\non this branch by widening the XS oracle's meter fields to txU8 (commit\\nc8497fd88). The port's matcher always metered into a u64 and held the full\\nvalue; the pre-fix oracle wrapped 8_411_414_528 mod 2^32 = 4_116_447_232 and\\nmanufactured a false divergence. Confirmed reproducing against the base SHA\\n38ca1d189384245dd9accfcc2f79763a3b8ec5cb and fixed at branch HEAD.\\n\\nThis case is a DISTINCT witness: unlike the sibling meter findings (which all\\nmatched), this one is a non-match, so it independently guards the full-width\\nmeter along the exhaustive-backtrack-to-failure path. The test needs neither\\nthe XS oracle nor the c/moddable submodule — it pins the port's own\\nfull-width meter for the exact reproducing case (matched=false,\\nmeter=8_411_414_528), the portable source-of-truth the oracle must agree with.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock non-match meter full-width (fuz…\",\"oid\":\"c8a7d0135ad750d931578693504cd3ccdc8441ce\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:09:17Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:09:24Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…flow (fuzz 637d760bc2e0278e)\\n\\nThe differential_regexp arm's 4-byte finding 637d760bc2e0278e folds into a\\ndeeply nested, backreference-heavy pattern whose 458132 backtracking steps\\ndrive the raw 16.16 match meter to 30024138752 (> u32::MAX). Same root cause\\nas 5d122a6fc10babd9 / 8275793bca439f6e / 407764ab1120ed1a: the XS oracle used\\nto truncate its 64-bit meter into a txU4, wrapping to 4254334976 and faking a\\ndivergence. The oracle-side 64-bit widening already landed on this branch; the\\nport was always correct. This test pins the port's full-width meter bit-exact\\nfor the exact reproducing case, oracle-free, guarding against any narrowing.\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock backref-heavy regexp meter over…\",\"oid\":\"1be01ad5c1f78191499eaed01d25dc59536c33e1\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:12:19Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:12:25Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…4de587e16bce32)\\n\\nContinuous ironhorse fuzz (target differential_source, toolchain\\nnightly-2026-08-15) minimized a 9-byte input that folds into the\\narithmetic program\\n\\n  (((~(true && true)) - ((780140544 - true) * (true + true)))\\n   * ((~(true && true)) - ((780140544 - true) * (true + true))))\\n\\nwhose value is 1560281088^2 = 8649 * 2^48 = 2434477073570463744, an\\nexactly-representable double. XS's fx_dtoa prints the exact 19-digit\\ninteger; ironhorse prints the ECMA-262 shortest round-tripping decimal\\n2434477073570464000 (matching V8/Node). Both parse to the identical\\ndouble, so this is the same oracle-rendering class as findings\\nd99d263fcf6ca7a7 / 5c29667cc15d6d93 / 7289e31013d074ec / 783be6e6106bad98,\\nalready suppressed on this branch by the numeric results_agree comparison.\\nNo port or harness change is needed for this input; add the regressions.\\n\\n- ironhorse-fuzz: replay the exact 9 bytes through the real\\n  differential_check and assert no divergence (load-bearing against the\\n  pinned XS oracle; fails if results_agree is reverted).\\n- ironhorse-vm: pin the reproducing value's number_to_ecma_string to the\\n  shortest decimal (the crate CI runs; no XS oracle / c/moddable needed),\\n  so the port can never be \\\"corrected\\\" to XS's non-shortest form.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse): regression-lock large-integer dtoa spelling (fuzz 28…\",\"oid\":\"92a7cb9cc0b5898cfb30a5211206d0bf18ca9052\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:16:11Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:16:17Z\",\"messageBody\":\"… 6fec81f3b42a99c1)\\n\\nThe 4-byte fuzz input 2c 2c 2c 64 folds into a nested new RegExp(...).source\\nwhose 1101-byte completion value overflowed the XS differential oracle's former\\n1024-byte capture buffer, so the oracle truncated its own reference value and\\nthe differential_regexp_surface target read the port's correct full result as a\\ndivergence. The port was never wrong; the causal fix is oracle-side and already\\nlanded for same-class finding 493390fc03979205. This submodule-free ironhorse-vm\\ntest replays the exact program (oracle-emitted bytecode + symbols) and asserts\\nthe VM renders the whole >1023-byte source string untruncated.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock regexp .source truncation (fuzz…\",\"oid\":\"4890a0a92737acf4397760f7182767e158e7f7e9\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:19:08Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:19:15Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…6f0b586a80019097)\\n\\nContinuous-Ironhorse-fuzz finding 6f0b586a80019097 (target\\ndifferential_regexp_surface, toolchain nightly-2026-08-15). The exact 5-byte\\ninput folds into a deeply nested `new RegExp(pat, \\\"\\\").source` whose completion\\nvalue is 1160 bytes. At the finding's project SHA 38ca1d18 the XS differential\\noracle captured the completion value into a fixed 1024-byte buffer and\\nstrncpy-truncated it to 1023 bytes; the harness then read the port's correct\\nfull 1160-byte result as a divergence and panicked. The port was never wrong.\\n\\nThis is a member of the already-fixed truncation class 493390fc03979205: the\\ncausal oracle-side fix (16 KiB capture buffer + honest skip on overflow) landed\\nafter the finding SHA, so no new code change is required — verified the exact\\ninput now checks clean (differential_check_with_symbols -> Ok) at the branch\\nhead. The load-bearing deliverable is the regression lock.\\n\\n- ironhorse-vm: finding_6f0b586a80019097_regexp_source.rs replays the finding's\\n  frozen bytecode+symbols (no XS oracle / no c/moddable submodule) and asserts\\n  the port renders the whole 1160-byte source, crossing the oracle's former\\n  1023-byte boundary, without panicking or truncating. This is the test the\\n  crate CI runs (`cargo test -p ironhorse-vm`).\\n- ironhorse-fuzz: finding_6f0b586a80019097_regexp_source_agrees replays the\\n  exact 5-byte input through the real differential_check_with_symbols and\\n  asserts no divergence (load-bearing — fails if the oracle fix is reverted).\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse): regression-lock long RegExp.source truncation (fuzz …\",\"oid\":\"3a695f3db5a1279c206e6dfb31b4317c02e0a243\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:19:44Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:19:53Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…zz 7152c1a9960a0688)\\n\\nContinuous ironhorse fuzz (target differential_source, toolchain\\nnightly-2026-08-15) minimized an 8-byte input `27 79 00 00 00 57 2d 08`\\n(sha256 f8b5e31e69a227500b3733aebdfffee49512debf2bb863c825991a4435652bc1)\\nthat folds into the arithmetic program\\n\\n  ((((1015021568 / true) * (377487360 + -89)) + (-(true + 377487360)))\\n   || 1015021568)\\n\\ni.e. `1015021568 * 377487271 - 377487361`, whose IEEE-754 double is the\\nexactly-representable value 383157721332973568 (bits 0x439544ffab840000).\\nXS's fx_dtoa renders it in a non-shortest 18-digit form\\n383157721332973570; ironhorse — like V8/Node and ECMA-262 §6.1.6.1.20's\\nshortest-round-tripping rule — renders 383157721332973600. Both parse to\\nthe identical double, so the engines agree on the value and diverge only\\non decimal spelling: the same oracle-rendering class as findings\\nd99d263fcf6ca7a7 / 5c29667cc15d6d93 / 7289e31013d074ec / 783be6e6106bad98\\n/ 284de587e16bce32, already suppressed on this branch by the numeric\\nresults_agree comparison. Reproduced at the fuzzed base 38ca1d18 under a\\nbyte-exact comparison (oracle \\\"383157721332973570\\\" vs ironhorse\\n\\\"383157721332973600\\\"); clean at HEAD. No port or harness change is\\nneeded for this input; add the regressions.\\n\\n- ironhorse-fuzz: replay the exact 8 bytes through the real\\n  differential_check and assert no divergence (load-bearing against the\\n  pinned XS oracle; fails if results_agree is reverted).\\n- ironhorse-vm: pin the reproducing value's number_to_ecma_string to the\\n  shortest decimal (the crate CI runs; no XS oracle / c/moddable needed),\\n  so the port can never be \\\"corrected\\\" to XS's non-shortest form.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse-fuzz): regression-lock large-integer dtoa spelling (fu…\",\"oid\":\"6f54f91a3366ffccd5205020a912a7c9c9fa8ad1\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:24:18Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"279080640+kriscendobot@users.noreply.github.com\",\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 4.8\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-08-31T03:24:52Z\",\"messageBody\":\"…77b0fc4a72d8d6)\\n\\nContinuous ironhorse fuzz (target differential_source, toolchain\\nnightly-2026-08-15) minimized a 3-byte input (3f f7 de) that folds into\\nthe arithmetic program\\n\\n  ((~((~2071986176) * (~2071986176)))\\n   * (~((~2071986176) * (~2071986176))))\\n\\ni.e. X * X where X = ~ToInt32((~2071986176)^2). The inner product\\n(-2071986177)^2 rounds to the double 4293126717679075328, whose ToInt32\\nis -150994944, so X = 150994943 and the program's value is 150994943^2 =\\n22799472811573248, an exactly-representable double. XS's fx_dtoa prints\\nthat exact 17-digit integer; ironhorse prints the ECMA-262 shortest\\nround-tripping decimal 22799472811573250 (matching V8/Node). Both parse\\nto the identical double, so this is the same oracle-rendering class as\\nfindings 284de587e16bce32 / d99d263fcf6ca7a7 / 5c29667cc15d6d93 /\\n7289e31013d074ec / 783be6e6106bad98, already suppressed on this branch by\\nthe numeric results_agree comparison. No port or harness change is needed\\nfor this input; add the regressions.\\n\\n- ironhorse-fuzz: replay the exact 3 bytes through the real\\n  differential_check and assert no divergence (load-bearing against the\\n  pinned XS oracle; fails if results_agree is reverted).\\n- ironhorse-vm: pin the reproducing value's number_to_ecma_string to the\\n  shortest decimal (the crate CI runs; no XS oracle / c/moddable needed),\\n  so the port can never be \\\"corrected\\\" to XS's non-shortest form.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"test(ironhorse): regression-lock large-integer dtoa spelling (fuzz 72…\",\"oid\":\"7205b4b3c236baf1a6a7a3b95ebd89dbfbee4c24\"}],\"headRefName\":\"ironhorse-fuzz-findings\",\"headRepositoryOwner\":{\"id\":\"U_kgDOEKJuwA\",\"name\":\"Kriscendo Bot\",\"login\":\"kriscendobot\"},\"isDraft\":true,\"number\":1088,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/endojs/endo-but-for-bots/actions/runs/33353793521/job/99371989910\",\"name\":\"browser-tests\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-08-31T03:25:20Z\",\"status\":\"IN_PROGRESS\",\"workflowName\":\"Browser Tests\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"conclusion\":\"\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/endojs/endo-but-for-bots/actions/runs/33353793517/job/99372035771\",\